# The Gradle wrapper is authored on Windows and executed on a Linux CI runner.
# Without this, a checkout with core.autocrlf=true can hand `gradlew` CRLF line
# endings, and `#!/bin/sh\r` fails with a "bad interpreter" error that reads like
# a missing file. Pinning the jar as binary keeps any text filter away from it.
* text=auto eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
*.jar binary
